---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REPO } from "../consts";
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms of use for the PhonePad website and software."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated 11 September 2026.</p>

      <h2>The software</h2>
      <p>
        PhonePad is free software under the
        <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">GNU General Public
        License, version 3 or later</a>. That licence, not this page, governs
        what you may do with the code. You may use it, study it, change it and
        share it; if you distribute a modified version you must share your
        source under the same terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        The wire protocol under <code>protocol/</code> is licensed separately
        under Apache-2.0, so anyone may write a compatible client or companion.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        PhonePad is provided <strong>as is, without warranty of any kind</strong>.
        This is the ordinary position for free software and it is stated in full
        in sections 15 and 16 of the GPL. Nobody is promising it will work, and
        nobody is liable if it does not.
      </p>
      <p>
        In plain terms: this is a side project given away for free. Use it
        because it is useful, not because anyone is accountable for it.
      </p>

      <h2>The name</h2>
      <p>
        "PhonePad" and "DynShift" are trademarks and are <em>not</em> covered by
        the software licence. You may fork the code freely; give your fork its
        own name. The
        <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/TRADEMARK.md`} rel="noopener">trademark policy</a>
        sets out what is fine without asking, which is most things.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        The content here is provided for information. It is kept accurate and
        every performance figure is measured rather than claimed, but it may
        still be wrong or out of date, and nothing on it is a guarantee.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site design, logo and written content are not covered by the GPL and
        are not licensed for reuse.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        PhonePad requires the <strong>ViGEmBus</strong> driver, which is
        separate software by different authors under its own licence and terms.
        Installing it is your decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        Xbox, Xbox Cloud Gaming, Game Pass and Windows are trademarks of
        Microsoft Corporation. PhonePad is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
        sponsored by Microsoft. Whether you may use PhonePad with a particular
        service is between you and that service.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not use PhonePad to break the rules of a game or service you are
        using — anti-cheat systems, competitive integrity and the terms of the
        platforms you play on are your responsibility. PhonePad presents an
        ordinary controller and does nothing to conceal itself, automate
        anything, or gain an advantage.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may change; the date above changes with them, and the
        history is public in the repository.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Open an issue on <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">the repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
